Z||000009||84Bill||06-08-2001||12:29 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by poupas:<P>   Well, as it happens, I was in Amsterdam for their queens birthday this year. On the second day I was there I was walking down a road and saw a Fiero GT. I was(first I was completely shocked) tempted to go say 'What the hell', but I passed, a little hung over. Cliff, do you know this person? Or is it you? If you live in Holland or Amsterdam, you heard about queensday, teargas at central station. I smelled some of that. Beautiful country.<BR><B>    Do you know of this red GT? Is there only one Fiero in Holland?<BR>    If you say yes this is the most bizarre 4 days on a forum ever!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LZeitgeist<P>This is not an off topic question IMO. No flames intended .   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> as far that the FieroLisa thread, yeah ok it got off topic but that was not his fault and besides that Cliff will intervine if he feels it's necessary to do so. So lets just leave the topc realavency disgression and intervention up to him.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> It helps to keep the peace and no one gets hurt feelings over it, Who is going to question Cliff's authority certainly not me. You on the other hand... well you get the idea.<p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-08-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000010||LZeitgeist||06-08-2001||03:59 PM||||84Bill - <P>I have no idea why my posts sound so harsh to you, but it's quite obvious we just don't see eye to eye on much here...<P>Cliff and I have always gotten along just great in the e-mails and notes we've passed between us, and the couple times he's seen a reason to question my actions or statements here, he's let me know through private e-mail and we've worked it out that way - the way that the Forum rules indicate. <P>Posting my opinion on a question someone else asks is just as legitimate as your opinion is, and I certainly don't see that it is in *any* way "questionings Cliff's authority", despite your efforts to make it sound as though that is what I intended to do.<P>If Cliff thinks I'm out of line, he'll let me know it in short order. It's not your place to tell me I'm out of line on his Forum any more that it is my place to dictate actions around here. However, I am *completely* allowed to offer my opinion on anything here, just as you are, or anyone else here is.  <P>I'm not sure whether you've got some unknown beef with me, or if we just have two completely different ways of expressing ourselves, but I wish we could figure out what the problem is and get back to communicating effectively again. I'd rather sever an acquaintanceship with someone I chat with than have to meticulously pick and choose every careful little word I say to them so they don't get upset at me... life's too short.  <P>As you say, no flames intended, in any way, shape or form - but I'm just trying to figure out if I'm *THAT* hard to understand when I post? I don't have these problems of miscommunications in any of the other forums and boards I frequent... why do they seem to show up here so much and so often? As far as I can tell, I don't have different styles of speech depending on what the subject happens to be...<P>I'm open to suggestions here...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||LZeitgeist||06-08-2001||04:40 PM||||Just for clarification here...<P>Poupas posted:<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I will ask something strange of you. Put my FieroLisa thread back on the general chat. Do you know why? Because, 'it is as amusing to fiero forum members as FEBO is to Holland tourists'. That is pretty amusing.<BR>What do you think of that?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I posted:<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>poupas - <BR>The section isn't 'General Chat' - the section is 'General Fiero Chat'.<P>Amusing or not, it doesn't belong anywhere except the OT section, and all members of the Forum can read whichever section they prefer at the moment.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I let him know that A) the non-Fiero 'general chat' aspects of things belonged in the forum into which Cliff had moved it, thereby *supporting*, not undermining, Cliff's authority here, and B) I let poupas know that even though his thread had been moved, it was still accessible to everyone here, so nothing was lost by its being moved.<P>Also, I was in conversation with Lisa just last night (when she IM'ed me to let me know she'd finally made it back to NC), and we were discussing at that time that it's kind of creepy being the subject of so many conversations that she's not an active member in. I was offering the thoughts along those line so she wouldn't have to.<P>Does this help clear things up a bit, 84Bill? <P>It's Friday... lemme buy you a beer?  <IMG SRC="http://fp.geocities.com/emotiondot/mug.gif"> ||||reg||1
