Z||000014||poupas||06-08-2001||08:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>I'm trying to figure out why FEBO would be funny to tourists. Perhaps it's because you have to open small windowed doors in the wall to get your food?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>   FEBO is amusing because it is the only place I have ever seen where you can buy burgers and 'kip' from a vending machine. Highly unusual.<BR>   When I was in A-Dam I was staying with a friend and roommates. Upon leaving I decided to get them a bottle to say thanks. Went down to the local Albert Hinds(grocery store), and do you know what I found and bought for them--Fiero martini. Cliff, you cant get that over here, you could probably make a lot of money importing that stuff to north america. To all the Fiero lovers!<P>||||reg||1
