Z||000016||Cliff Pennock||06-08-2001||09:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by poupas:<BR><B>FEBO is amusing because it is the only place I have ever seen where you can buy burgers and 'kip' from a vending machine. Highly unusual.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, that's pretty normal here. Febo is probably the only one you have seen, but almost every <I>snackbar</I> (that's what they are called here) has those vending machines. But have you tasted some of the finer dutch snacks like <I>frikandellen</I>, <I>kroketten</I> or <I>kaas-soufflés</I>? You really don't want to know what's in them, but them sure are tasty!<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>When I was in A-Dam I was staying with a friend and roommates. Upon leaving I decided to get them a bottle to say thanks. Went down to the local Albert Hinds(grocery store), and do you know what I found and bought for them--Fiero martini. Cliff, you cant get that over here, you could probably make a lot of money importing that stuff to north america. To all the Fiero lovers!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I know, I started a thread about it a long time ago.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/martini.jpg"> <P>Oh, and by the way, it's Albert <B>Heyn</B> and not <B>Hinds</B>!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
